{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ3AG1JptgBZeoWe1JUz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't give you a full summary of the regulatory risks. My tools can't open the text of the 10-K. They can only tell me whether a word or phrase appears in it. So what follows is a list of the regulatory topics I could confirm are mentioned, plus a few I checked that aren't. I can't describe what the filing actually says about any of them.\n\n**Filing:** Paylocity's FY2024 10-K, for the year ended June 30, 2024, filed August 2, 2024. Paylocity also filed 10-Ks on August 6, 2025 and August 5, 2026. Both are after the May 16, 2025 cutoff, so I didn't use them.\n\n**Topics the 10-K mentions:**\n1. **Money transmitter rules:** The phrase \"money transmitter\" appears. This probably relates to Paylocity holding and moving client money for payroll and payments, but I couldn't read the passage to confirm.\n2. **Data privacy:** The \"California Consumer Privacy Act\" is named. This suggests the filing discusses the risk of state privacy laws governing the employee data Paylocity handles.\n3. **Artificial intelligence:** \"Artificial intelligence\" appears. Many 10-Ks now flag new and changing AI rules as a risk, but I couldn't confirm that this mention is about regulation rather than products or competition.\n4. **General laws, regulation, payroll tax and privacy:** A search on \"regulation laws risk payroll tax privacy\" matched this filing. Those words weren't searched as an exact phrase, so this only shows that each word appears somewhere in the document.\n\n**Topics not found as exact phrases:** \"Affordable Care Act\" and \"anti-money laundering\" don't appear. Paylocity may still cover those areas using other wording.\n\n**Gaps:** I couldn't read the Item 1A risk factor text, Paylocity's own description of each risk, or how likely or costly the company thinks each one is. To get a real summary, read \"Risk Factors\" in Item 1A and the \"Government Regulation\" part of Item 1 in the filing linked below.\n\n**Sources**\n- Form 10-K (FY ended June 30, 2024), filed 2024-08-02, accession 0001591698-24-000151: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1591698/000159169824000151/pcty-20240630.htm"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":8757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e19ae88d-f0ac-4d9b-8cea-1793c9a55710","uuid":"093b7fe0-dafe-4ee4-a7a2-1ea140f4cfd3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:12:02.829Z","request_id":"req_011CgQ3AFmuxWu17Tm6LHvSQ"}
